uence, exact-values, read-only-code. Learner actions: read, recall, inspect, compare. Evidence outputs: visible-claim, fixed-steps, exact-lookup, code-example. Limitations: no learner-controlled state, no code execution.", "callout": "create-content: Author static prose and layout blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, table, code, compare, and grid. Use when a lecture needs narrative or nominal lookup rather than a structural diagram, interactive simulation, quiz, or code runtime. Affordances: prose, fixed-comparison, fixed-sequence, exact-values, read-only-code. Learner actions: read, recall, inspect, compare. Evidence outputs: visible-claim, fixed-steps, exact-lookup, code-example. Limitations: no learner-controlled state, no code execution.", "formula": "create-content: Author static prose and layout blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, table, code, compare, and grid. Use when a lecture needs narrative or nominal lookup rather than a structural diagram, interactive simulation, quiz, or code runtime. Affordances: prose, fixed-comparison, fixed-sequence, exact-values, read-only-code. Learner actions: read, recall, inspect, compare. Evidence outputs: visible-claim, fixed-steps, exact-lookup, code-example. Limitations: no learner-controlled state, no code execution.", "table": "create-content: Author static prose and layout blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, table, code, compare, and grid. Use when a lecture needs narrative or nominal lookup rather than a structural diagram, interactive simulation, quiz, or code runtime. Affordances: prose, fixed-comparison, fixed-sequence, exact-values, read-only-code. Learner actions: read, recall, inspect, compare. Evidence outputs: visible-claim, fixed-steps, exact-lookup, code-example. Limitations: no learner-controlled state, no code execution.", "code": "create-content: Author static prose and layout blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, table, code, compare, and grid. Use when a lecture needs narrative or nominal lookup rather than a structural diagram, interactive simulation, quiz, or code runtime. Affordances: prose, fixed-comparison, fixed-sequence, exact-values, read-only-code. Learner actions: read, recall, inspect, compare. Evidence outputs: visible-claim, fixed-steps, exact-lookup, code-example. Limitations: no learner-controlled state, no code execution.", "compare": "create-content: Author static prose and layout blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, table, code, compare, and grid. Use when a lecture needs narrative or nominal lookup rather than a structural diagram, interactive simulation, quiz, or code runtime. Affordances: prose, fixed-comparison, fixed-sequence, exact-values, read-only-code. Learner actions: read, recall, inspect, compare. Evidence outputs: visible-claim, fixed-steps, exact-lookup, code-example. Limitations: no learner-controlled state, no code execution.", "grid": "create-content: Author static prose and layout blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, table, code, compare, and grid. Use when a lecture needs narrative or nominal lookup rather than a structural diagram, interactive simulation, quiz, or code runtime. Affordances: prose, fixed-comparison, fixed-sequence, exact-values, read-only-code. Learner actions: read, recall, inspect, compare. Evidence outputs: visible-claim, fixed-steps, exact-lookup, code-example. Limitations: no learner-controlled state, no code execution.", "flow": "create-diagram: Author structural diagram, graph, flow, and timeline blocks for a LectureDoc lecture. Use graph for explicit named edges, branching, hierarchy, or convergence; diagram when a fixed shape carries the relationship; flow for one simple linear chain; timeline only for events with explicit times or stages. Use state-sim when understanding depends on intermediate states or transformations rather than a fixed relationship. Affordances: spatial-structure, node-edge-relations, hierarchy, sequence, chronology. Learner actions: inspect, trace, compare. Evidence outputs: named-relations, fixed-structure, linear-sequence, chronology. Limitations: fixed-state-only, no-coordinate-proof, no-hidden-transition.", "timeline": "create-diagram: Author structural diagram, graph, flow, and timeline blocks for a LectureDoc lecture. Use graph for explicit named edges, branching, hierarchy, or convergence; diagram when a fixed shape carries the relationship; flow for one simple linear chain; timeline only for events with explicit times or stages. Use state-sim when understanding depends on intermediate states or transformations rather than a fixed relationship. Affordances: spatial-structure, node-edge-relations, hierarchy, sequence, chronology. Learner actions: inspect, trace, compare. Evidence outputs: named-relations, fixed-structure, linear-sequence, chronology. Limitations: fixed-state-only, no-coordinate-proof, no-hidden-transition.", "diagram": "create-diagram: Author structural diagram, graph, flow, and timeline blocks for a LectureDoc lecture. Use graph for explicit named edges, branching, hierarchy, or convergence; diagram when a fixed shape carries the relationship; flow for one simple linear chain; timeline only for events with explicit times or stages. Use state-sim when understanding depends on intermediate states or transformations rather than a fixed relationship. Affordances: spatial-structure, node-edge-relations, hierarchy, sequence, chronology. Learner actions: inspect, trace, compare. Evidence outputs: named-relations, fixed-structure, linear-sequence, chronology. Limitations: fixed-state-only, no-coordinate-proof, no-hidden-transition.", "graph": "create-diagram: Author structural diagram, graph, flow, and timeline blocks for a LectureDoc lecture. Use graph for explicit named edges, branching, hierarchy, or convergence; diagram when a fixed shape carries the relationship; flow for one simple linear chain; timeline only for events with explicit times or stages. Use state-sim when understanding depends on intermediate states or transformations rather than a fixed relationship. Affordances: spatial-structure, node-edge-relations, hierarchy, sequence, chronology. Learner actions: inspect, trace, compare. Evidence outputs: named-relations, fixed-structure, linear-sequence, chronology. Limitations: fixed-state-only, no-coordinate-proof, no-hidden-transition.", "freeform": "create-freeform: Author a freeform block for a LectureDoc lecture — the long-tail fallback for a visual relationship that none of the formal block types can express, drawn as inline SVG/HTML restricted to theme colour tokens. Reach for it only after checking the structured types: graph covers trees, DAGs and branching flowcharts; chart covers data; diagram covers fixed shapes; grid and sim.widget cover custom layouts and interactive pieces. When it genuinely is the right tool it now renders as normal page content, so use it without hedging.", "geometry-sim": "create-geometry-sim: Plan a spatial constraint simulation for a LectureDoc lecture. Use when coordinate mapping, dragging, boundaries, vectors, geometric construction, or spatial invariants are themselves the learning evidence. Do not use merely because a state diagram has positioned nodes; AVL rotations remain state-sim. The final block lowers to sim.widget. Affordances: drag, coordinate-map, constraint, construction, spatial-transform. Learner actions: manipulate, construct, predict, inspect. Evidence outputs: coordinate-change, constraint-preservation, spatial-invariant. Limitations: not-decorative-layout, not-discrete-structure, not-code-execution.", "stats": "create-infographic: Author stats blocks for a LectureDoc lecture. Use only to spotlight 2-6 standalone key numbers whose individual magnitude is the evidence; use chart for trends, distributions, or correlations and create-diagram for structural relationships. Affordances: standalone-metrics, fixed-state. Learner actions: inspect, compare. Evidence outputs: key-number. Limitations: no-trends, no-structural-relations, no-unsourced-numbers.", "model-sim": "create-model-sim: Plan a parameterized model simulation for a LectureDoc lecture. Use when learners must change real parameters and observe a recomputed quantitative consequence, compare model regimes, or inspect deterministic or stochastic causal behavior. Use chart for a fixed dataset and state-sim for discrete algorithm steps. Lowers to the shared sim runtime. Affordances: parameter-control, recompute, comparison, stochastic, history. Learner actions: manipulate, predict, calculate, compare. Evidence outputs: parameter-output-map, regime-change, quantitative-cause. Limitations: not-fixed-dataset, not-code-execution, not-discrete-structure.", "quiz": "create-quiz: Author a quiz block for a LectureDoc lecture — objective (multiple-choice, auto-graded) or subjective (open discussion prompt). Reach for it whenever a page should check understanding or provoke reflection rather than only present — at least one per lecture is encouraged. Objective for a checkable fact/skill, subjective for open-ended thinking. Affordances: elicited-response, auto-grading, misconception-diagnosis. Learner actions: predict, calculate, judge, explain. Evidence outputs: student-answer, correctness-feedback, explanation. Limitations: one assessment chain per block.", "state-sim": "create-state-sim: Plan a discrete state simulation for a LectureDoc lecture. Use whenever learning evidence depends on an algorithm's intermediate states, stepwise execution, tree/graph/array mutation, structural transformation, replay, or before-to-after mapping. AVL rotations and data-structure updates belong here even though nodes have positions. The final block lowers to sim.widget. Affordances: state-transition, step, reset, playback, history, comparison. Learner actions: trace, predict, manipulate, construct. Evidence outputs: intermediate-state, transition-sequence, before-after-map. Limitations: not-static-snapshot, not-code-execution, not-coordinate-constraint."}, "currentBrief": {"objective": "学生能识别 RR 不平衡模式，并描述左旋的步骤和结果", "learningAction": "trace", "requiredEvidence": "学生能画出左旋前后的树结构", "keyClaim": "RR 不平衡通过一次左旋恢复平衡，与 LL 右旋对称", "misconception": "左旋和右旋是不同的操作", "visualTask": "展示左旋时节点指针的重新连接，突出子树 T2 的归属变化", "evidencePolicy": "provided"}, "currentScene": {"id": "rr-rotation", "kind": "content", "headline": "RR 不平衡与左旋", "lead": "插入 1,2,3：节点 1 的平衡因子变为 -2，触发 RR 型左旋——与右旋对称。", "notes": "演示 RR 不平衡和左旋，强调对称性", "blocks": [{"type": "sim", "engine": "widget", "html": "<style>
* { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
html, body { width: 100%; height: 100%; min-width: 0; min-height: 0; overflow: hidden; }
body { font-family: var(--font-sans, ui-monospace, 'Cascadia Mono', Consolas, monospace); background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink); }
.widget { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: flex; flex-direction: column; padding: 12px 16px; gap: 8px; }
.title { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--text2); letter-spacing: 0.02em; }
.controls { display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; }
.controls button { font-family: inherit; font-size: 13px; padding: 6px 16px; border: 1px solid var(--line, rgba(90,78,128,.25)); border-radius: 8px; background: var(--bg2); color: var(--ink); cursor: pointer; transition: all .15s; }
.controls button:hover { background: var(--accent); color:var(--card); border-color: var(--accent); }
.controls button:active { transform: scale(.97); }
.controls button:disabled { opacity: .4; cursor: default; transform: none; }
.stage { flex: 1; min-height: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; background: var(--bg2); border: 1px solid var(--line, rgba(90,78,128,.10)); border-radius: 12px; position: relative; overflow: hidden; }
.stage svg { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; }
.readout { display: flex; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; font-size: 12px; color: var(--text2); padding: 4px 0; }
.readout span { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.readout .label { color: var(--text2); }
.readout .value { font-weight: 500; color: var(--ink); }
.pulse-ring { animation: pulse 1.5s ease-in-out infinite; }
@keyframes pulse {
  0%, 100% { opacity: 1; }
  50% { opacity: .5; }
}
</style>
<div class="widget">
  <div class="title">RR 不平衡与左旋</div>
  <div class="controls">
    <button id="stepBtn" onclick="nextStep()">单步推进</button>
    <button id="resetBtn" onclick="resetStep()">重置</button>
  </div>
  <div class="stage" id="stage">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 400 200" id="treeSvg"></svg>
  </div>
  <div class="readout">
    <span><span class="label">步骤</span> <span class="value" id="stepDisplay">0</span></span>
    <span><span class="label">根节点</span> <span class="value" id="rootDisplay">1</span></span>
    <span><span class="label">平衡因子</span> <span class="value" id="bfDisplay">0</span></span>
  </div>
</div>
<script>
let step = 0;
const svg = document.getElementById('treeSvg');
const stepDisplay = document.getElementById('stepDisplay');
const rootDisplay = document.getElementById('rootDisplay');
const bfDisplay = document.getElementById('bfDisplay');
const stepBtn = document.getElementById('stepBtn');
const resetBtn = document.getElementById('resetBtn');

function drawTree(s) {
  svg.innerHTML = '';
  const ns = 'http://www.w3.org/2000/svg';
  let nodes = [];
  let edges = [];
  let bf = 0;
  let rootVal = 1;
  let highlightNode = null;

  if (s === 0) {
    // 仅根节点 1
    nodes = [{x:200, y:80, val:1, bf:0}];
    rootVal = 1;
    bf = 0;
  } else if (s === 1) {
    // 插入 2，节点 1 BF=-1
    nodes = [
      {x:200, y:60, val:1, bf:-1},
      {x:280, y:120, val:2, bf:0}
    ];
    edges = [{x1:200, y1:80, x2:280, y2:120}];
    rootVal = 1;
    bf = -1;
  } else if (s === 2) {
    // 插入 3，节点 1 BF=-2（红色）
    nodes = [
      {x:200, y:40, val:1, bf:-2, highlight:true},
      {x:280, y:100, val:2, bf:-1},
      {x:340, y:160, val:3, bf:0}
    ];
    edges = [
      {x1:200, y1:60, x2:280, y2:100},
      {x1:280, y1:120, x2:340, y2:160}
    ];
    rootVal = 1;
    bf = -2;
    highlightNode = 1;
  } else if (s === 3) {
    // 左旋后，根为 2，左 1 右 3，所有 BF=0
    nodes = [
      {x:200, y:60, val:2, bf:0},
      {x:120, y:120, val:1, bf:0},
      {x:280, y:120, val:3, bf:0}
    ];
    edges = [
      {x1:200, y1:80, x2:120, y2:120},
      {x1:200, y1:80, x2:280, y2:120}
    ];
    rootVal = 2;
    bf = 0;
  }

  // 画边
  for (const e of edges) {
    const line = document.createElementNS(ns, 'line');
    line.setAttribute('x1', e.x1);
    line.setAttribute('y1', e.y1);
    line.setAttribute('x2', e.x2);
    line.setAttribute('y2', e.y2);
    line.setAttribute('stroke', 'var(--line, rgba(90,78,128,.3))');
    line.setAttribute('stroke-width', '2');
    svg.appendChild(line);
  }

  // 画节点
  for (const n of nodes) {
    const g = document.createElementNS(ns, 'g');
    const circle = document.createElementNS(ns, 'circle');
    circle.setAttribute('cx', n.x);
    circle.setAttribute('cy', n.y);
    circle.setAttribute('r', '22');
    let fill = 'var(--bg2)';
    let stroke = 'var(--line, rgba(90,78,128,.3))';
    if (n.highlight) {
      fill = 'var(--accent)';
      stroke = 'var(--accent)';
      circle.setAttribute('stroke-width', '3');
      circle.classList.add('pulse-ring');
    }
    circle.setAttribute('fill', fill);
    circle.setAttribute('stroke', stroke);
    circle.setAttribute('stroke-width', '2');
    g.appendChild(circle);

    const text = document.createElementNS(ns, 'text');
    text.setAttribute('x', n.x);
    text.setAttribute('y', n.y + 5);
    text.setAttribute('text-anchor', 'middle');
    text.setAttribute('font-size', '16');
    text.setAttribute('font-weight', '500');
    text.setAttribute('fill', 'var(--ink)');
    text.textContent = n.val;
    g.appendChild(text);

    // 平衡因子标注
    const bfText = document.createElementNS(ns, 'text');
    bfText.setAttribute('x', n.x + 30);
    bfText.setAttribute('y', n.y - 8);
    bfText.setAttribute('font-size', '12');
    bfText.setAttribute('fill', n.highlight ? 'var(--accent)' : 'var(--text2)');
    bfText.setAttribute('font-weight', n.highlight ? '600' : '400');
    bfText.textContent = 'BF=' + n.bf;
    g.appendChild(bfText);

    svg.appendChild(g);
  }

  // 更新读数
  stepDisplay.textContent = s;
  rootDisplay.textContent = rootVal;
  bfDisplay.textContent = bf;
  if (bf === -2) {
    bfDisplay.style.color = 'var(--accent)';
    bfDisplay.style.fontWeight = '600';
  } else {
    bfDisplay.style.color = 'var(--ink)';
    bfDisplay.style.fontWeight = '500';
  }
}

function nextStep() {
  if (step < 3) {
    step++;
    drawTree(step);
  }
  stepBtn.disabled = step >= 3;
}

function resetStep() {
  step = 0;
  drawTree(step);
  stepBtn.disabled = false;
}

// 初始绘制
drawTree(0);
</script>", "spec": {"core_insight": "学生能识别 RR 不平衡模式，并描述左旋的步骤和结果", "render_medium": "svg", "render_medium_reason": "由规划阶段的证据形态确定", "aesthetic_direction": "host-calm", "direction_reason": "LectureDoc host palette; preserve lab-dark only in layout, motion, and signature detail", "palette": ["var(--bg)", "var(--bg2)", "var(--ink)", "var(--text2)", "var(--accent)", "var(--line)"], "signature_detail": "失衡节点用红色脉冲光环标记", "layout_pattern": "stage+readout-row", "layout_skeleton": "title / compact controls / full-width stage / readout row", "state_model": [{"name": "step", "type": "int", "range_or_values": "0..3", "initial": 0}], "interactions": [{"trigger": "单步按钮", "effect": "推进一步并调用 update()"}], "render_contract": "step 递增时，根据 step 值绘制对应状态的树", "update": "step 递增时，根据 step 值绘制对应状态的树", "initial_paint": "step=0，仅根节点 1", "visible_encodings": [{"quantity": "当前步骤的树结构", "mark": "节点+连线", "where": "主舞台"}, {"quantity": "失衡节点的平衡因子", "mark": "红色高亮", "where": "节点旁"}], "comparison_states": [], "interaction_loop": {"action": "单步按钮", "model_update": "step 递增时，根据 step 值绘制对应状态的树", "visible_change": "当前步骤的树结构; 失衡节点的平衡因子", "history": "不保留前态，每次显示当前状态", "reset": "step 置 0"}, "math_model": {"formula": "none", "screen_mapping": "not applicable", "invariants": []}, "verification_cases": [{"input": "step=0", "expected": "仅根节点 1"}, {"input": "step=1", "expected": "插入 2，节点 1 BF=-1"}, {"input": "step=2", "expected": "插入 3，节点 1 BF=-2（红色）"}, {"input": "step=3", "expected": "左旋后，根为 2，左 1 右 3，所有 BF=0"}], "profile": "state", "source_aesthetic_direction": "lab-dark"}, "id": "s4b0"}], "layout": {"kind": "full"}}, "qualityIssues": ["质量审查失败: "]}
